the screen view changes to become like one giant screen where maybe, you know, the animation

00:33:00.640 --> 00:33:01.780
is a little more detailed or something.

00:33:01.780 --> 00:33:06.520
And you have more, you know, it's not the same restrictions and layout as the rest of

00:33:06.520 --> 00:33:10.400
the game. It's this unique scenario where you're both now registered in the same room.

00:33:10.820 --> 00:33:15.120
And I'm thinking like, you know, because we just played racket attack that switch between

00:33:15.120 --> 00:33:17.320
serving and the rest of the game.

00:33:17.340 --> 00:33:20.860
You know, it's like you kind of hope that like it would just make that jump to open up

00:33:20.860 --> 00:33:22.160
a few more opportunities.

00:33:23.140 --> 00:33:27.080
Not that you guys haven't sold me on your argument for why the combat being simple is fine.

00:33:27.480 --> 00:33:33.720
I just think like that was a moment for something a little extra in the in the cartoony department

00:33:33.720 --> 00:33:38.980
to, you know, like that is such a cartoony thing that you I guess like maybe there is

00:33:38.980 --> 00:33:44.700
something slapstick about just two spies beating each other over the head, like popping each

00:33:44.700 --> 00:33:48.160
other. Maybe that is funny, but I would have expected something else.

00:33:48.480 --> 00:33:54.220
Yeah, I do think that and I don't know if I'd ever if I'd make this argument in any other

00:33:54.220 --> 00:34:03.780
context. But if you make the combat in this game too good, you're undercutting everything else.

00:34:03.960 --> 00:34:07.780
Like if that were the case and you're playing with another person and you thought that the

00:34:07.780 --> 00:34:13.680
combat was more fun than this cat and mouse thing that you're doing, you would just you just

00:34:13.680 --> 00:34:18.620
rush at each other and kind of ignore trapping and ignore everything else.

00:34:18.740 --> 00:34:24.240
I think that if you made the combat too good, it wouldn't it would be a completely different

00:34:24.240 --> 00:34:25.700
game. I think that's a great point.

00:34:25.900 --> 00:34:29.000
I want to mention something interesting about the about the combat, though.

00:34:29.180 --> 00:34:31.800
The it's not a complaint or a praise.

00:34:31.800 --> 00:34:36.980
It's just it's just weird that, you know, if you're if you're playing on the top half

00:34:36.980 --> 00:34:41.360
of the screen and your opponents on the bottom half, when you end up in the same room together,

00:34:41.800 --> 00:34:43.860
one of you will move to their screen.

00:34:44.820 --> 00:34:50.180
Yes, like you won't both be but the room won't be displayed on both sides of the screen.

00:34:50.320 --> 00:34:53.380
You'll just whoever was in the room first will stay on their side of the screen.

00:34:53.580 --> 00:34:56.300
And if I'm on the top of the screen and I go into a room that you're in, I'll appear

00:34:56.300 --> 00:34:59.680
on the bottom screen and there'll be nobody in the top screen for a second.

00:34:59.680 --> 00:35:03.000
I thought that was interesting and I don't know if that was a technical limitation or

00:35:03.000 --> 00:35:04.780
if that was a creative decision.

00:35:05.260 --> 00:35:11.060
I think it's I think it's sort of and I don't don't quote me on this, but I think it's also

00:35:11.060 --> 00:35:17.580
supposed to just hide what your inventory is like you kind of have the jump on this person

00:35:17.580 --> 00:35:19.160
so you can see what he has.

00:35:20.720 --> 00:35:25.660
But he doesn't see how like what what key items you have.

00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:30.280
And I don't know why that that only is a thing when you're in the same room fighting.

00:35:30.900 --> 00:35:33.580
But there was some reason in the manual.

00:35:33.800 --> 00:35:37.760
I just don't remember. But you can't you wouldn't be able to see what item they have because as soon as you end up

00:35:37.760 --> 00:35:41.780
in the same room together, all of your items vanish and go in and get hidden into one of

00:35:41.780 --> 00:35:42.980
the rooms. Right.

00:35:43.800 --> 00:35:45.060
True. That's true.

